      "body": "### Environment\n\nplayground\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\n@typescript-eslint/parser\n\n### What did you do?\n\n```ts\n/* eslint no-unassigned-vars: [\"warn\"] */\n\nlet x!: string;\n\neval(\"x = 'a string'\");\n\nx.toString();\n```\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nno report\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nlint report: 'x' is always 'undefined' because it's never assigned.\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nIMO this shouldn't report since the definite assignment assertion tells TS \"I promise you this is assigned by the team you read it\"\n\nObserved in the wild: https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/blob/05014ff054cfa336c8ca48bac08deec3225675ab/packages/eslint-plugin/tools/generate-breaking-changes.mts#L22-L27",
