      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "### Environment\n\n\nGithub Actions Runner\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nOther\n\n### What did you do?\n\n\nUnrelated code change, see https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20000\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nIntegration tests not fail\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nIntegration tests fail:\n\n```text\nRun npm run check:tsc\n\n> neostandard@0.12.2 check:tsc\n> tsc\n\nError: lib/ts.js(25,21): error TS2339: Property 'rules' does not exist on type 'CompatiblePlugin'.\nError: lib/ts.js(49,66): error TS2339: Property 'rules' does not exist on type 'CompatiblePlugin'.\n```\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://github.com/eslint/eslint/actions/runs/17081157353/job/48435110028?pr=20020\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nFrom the error messages, this appears to be due to https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/pull/11475 being recently released (https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/releases/tag/v8.40.0)\n\nHowever, I'm not familiar enough with the eslint repo to know how to debug or even run the integration tests.",
